cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Wer diese Arbeit verwendet, zitiert sie bitte wie folgt."
title: "Reformulation - Polykontexturale Logik in Lean 4"
abstract: >-
  The eleventh edition of a working paper that reformulates Gotthard Günther's polycontextural
  logic in Lean 4 and Mathlib.
  Part A has a new centre and proves three things about negation cycles as Günther writes them
  down. Günther's family formed from the distributions 10-9-5 and 5-9-10 is, on the
  distributions, exactly one orbit of the reversal. Reversal and sense of rotation of a full
  cycle coincide for three values and never from four values on. And the step to one more value
  carries the reversal along when it changes the direction in which it shifts. Added to these
  are the theorems that carry the three in detail, and a calculation at the tables of an early
  textbook of change ringers. New in Part A are a posit, that we read the cycles as heirs
  of a sentence Günther wrote in 1957, and an assignment that carries its centre: what
  withstands every aspect of a circle we call, with Günther's word, general. Whether that has to
  do with what Günther calls intersubjective generality is the question on which the edition
  ends; the corpus contains no I and no Thou.
  The report proves or measures five further things. A conjecture of the tenth edition is
  decided. Kaehr's calculus of 1981, corrected in one line, captures exactly the fibres; against
  Günther's values it is neither sound nor complete. Four of his tableau rules of 1993,
  supplemented by one from 1981, are, against a semantics we have chosen, sound in a weak sense and
  not complete. Meixl's tables are Günther's. A map of the corpus shows where contextures have a
  validity of their own. Whatever is said beyond that is an assignment, a reading or a
  synopsis, and is called so.
  The errors in the list of errors were found by roles of instances of one model family, not by
  independent checkers; what a model systematically gets wrong, all of its roles can miss. Two
  check independently today: the proof environment, for the theorems and not for the marks and
  quotations, and the author of the project. The list shows that the roles catch a lot; that
  they are independent, it does not show.
  No machine checks the marks, readings, assignments and quotations; they are set so that they can be checked,
  quotations with source and page. Whoever does so is welcome, and what proves to be an error goes
  into the list of errors, with the finder's name if they wish. Findings reach us on X, @PolyContextual.
type: software
